PARAGRAPH:
<<<
To accelerate the discovery of resilient metastable materials, we introduce a machine learning framework designed to efficiently navigate the TMD chemical space and identify promising candidates for synthesis. Our approach bypasses the direct and computationally demanding calculation of elastic properties for every hypothetical structure. Instead, we train a model to predict a key descriptor of mechanical behavior—Pugh's ratio, $G/K$, the ratio of the shear modulus $G$ to the bulk modulus $K$—from a small set of fundamental electronic and structural features. By learning the complex, non-linear relationships between these accessible descriptors and mechanical robustness, our model can rapidly screen large databases of materials to pinpoint those with a high likelihood of being both functional and durable.

>>>

