The foundation of our study is a dataset comprising 202 transition-metal dichalcogenides (TMDs), for which structural and electronic properties were pre-computed. The primary target variable for our machine learning model is Pugh's ratio, defined as the ratio of the shear modulus to the bulk modulus ($G/K$). We use the Voigt-Reuss-Hill (VRH) averages for both moduli, yielding the target variable $G_{vrh}/K_{vrh}$. Elastic tensor data required to compute this ratio were available for a subset of 90 materials.

